-text `evidence` string. A structured date field, something like `invalid_from` or `valid_to`, would let later queries tell what was true before and after the change without having to parse prose. `update` has `valid_from` for backdating a new claim, but `challenge` has nothing like it for closing the old one.\n\n2. **There's no lightweight way to record a partial replacement.** I knew the new fact (\"staging uses its own bucket\") but not the bucket's name, so I only challenged the old memory and offered to update it later. `create` with `supersedes` would have worked, but it treats the new memory as complete. A way to mark a replacement as provisional, or to attach a \"pending confirmation: bucket name unknown\" note to the challenged memory, would let the next session see that the correction is half done. Without it, the next session sees only a challenged hazard and nothing that says staging is now separate.\n\nOtherwise, the hook-injected context and the tools I used (ToolSearch to load `challenge`, then `challenge` itself) did what I needed."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 10778, "cache_read_input_tokens": 15203, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 10778}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [{"type": "thinking_dropped", "path": "messages.2.content.0", "reason": "prefix_binding_mismatch"}, {"type": "thinking_dropped", "path": "messages.8.content.0", "reason": "prefix_binding_mismatch"}], "diagnostics": {"cache_miss_reason": {"type": "tools_changed", "cache_missed_input_tokens": 24200}}, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "b6364f98-daa6-4c00-bcd5-d9c5e536415f", "uuid": "41b8d2cd-fd3e-4137-bb2c-36211cedcc27", "timestamp": "2026-10-02T00:24:38.015Z", "request_id": "req_011CfcTZPrMfZTk76bdz3ZfB"}, {"